# Line-ending policy: the repository stores LF, and every working tree gets LF.
#
# Without this file the behaviour depends on each developer's personal
# `core.autocrlf`, so a Windows and a macOS checkout of the same commit differ.
# That per-machine asymmetry is what produced the recurring
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" warnings, and it is
# the same class of Windows/POSIX divergence that hid the gate defects fixed in
# a9bf74d. `eol=lf` removes the conversion entirely rather than configuring it:
# no conversion, no warning, and identical bytes on both platforms.
#
# Every text blob in this repository was already LF when this file was added, so
# it changes no committed content — only the working-tree checkout and the rules
# applied from here on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never inspected, never converted, never diffed as text.
*.dacpac binary
*.png    binary
*.vsix   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
